      ],
      "summary": "`@tangleai/os` can be used from another repository without a registry. Every release keeps the package tarball, a one-file module side (`connectToOs` with its dependencies inside, for a page on any foundation) and a manifest of their hashes, protocol and Jaren foundation under `releases/os/`, and the desktop site serves the same files under `os/`. The package now depends on Jaren alone. `kernel.operations()` lists what a caller may call as plain data, for an application with its own agent runtime. Migration: `kernel.tools()` builds its tools with the host's tool builder, so pass one when creating the kernel: `createKernel({ tools })` with `import * as tools from \"@tangleai/agents/toolbox\"`; without one it refuses with `OS0301`.",
      "id": "os-from-a-submodule"
    }
